                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "238217457",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561199553706177",
                            "num_reviews": 7,
                            "playtime_forever": 3753,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 704,
                            "playtime_at_review": 2372,
                            "last_played": 1793834015
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I love this game. It has been my primary game for about a month now, and it stems from a few things. The diver gameplay is horrifyingly fun. Some games can end in seconds with sharks killing everyone in minutes, and others come down to the wire and really challenge both sides. As a shark, it can be frustrating, as some diver weapons are incredibly good in the right hands. However an evenly matched game can be incredibly fun, and sometimes a death is almost comedic. Lastly, cosmetics are (in part) free. While some are locked behind a bundle, most are found on either the market or in the free chests, which unlike other games don't require keys, and can't be traded. Further more, there are crafting tokens which can be used to create chests and certain cosmetics, each related to a certain event or time of year. I hope to see this game have a revival and hit new peaks, especially in a world filled with microtransactions, where this game feels like a refresher. New players will struggle, I'm sure, but don't let that deter you. This game doesn't take long to get a grip, and while you may get stomped here and there, let it be a reminder that you can always improve.",
